O:8:"stdClass":8:{s:5:"title";s:62:"Meet Kate Allstadt, self-described “present-day geologist”";s:4:"link";s:96:"https://environment.uw.edu/news/2014/06/meet-kate-allstadt-self-described-present-day-geologist/";s:11:"description";s:461:"<div>What would you do in a big earthquake? Do you know how your neighborhood would fare? Would the ground beneath your house hold firm, or turn into liquid, or break loose in a landslide? If you had a few seconds or minutes warning, how would you prepare knowing a devastating earthquake was about to be unleashed?
